# A worded chain step inside a green-thread group. The two members run as
# fibers, so the rescue's subject is executed by the scheduler rather than by
# the flat chain loop, and that is a different path on every engine.
#
# The arm discards the reason, which is what lets all three engines read one
# golden: a page has no filesystem and says so in its own words, native says
# the file is not there, and `rescued` is the answer either way.
import "std/os"

fn told (err _)
  "rescued"

fn told v
  "{v}"

pub play =
  print "start"
  >>
  rescue (os/read_file "no-such-file.txt") told . print
  print "beside it"
